{
  "title": "Pseudohypoparathyroidism",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/basic-science/9029/pseudohypoparathyroidism",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Jun 18 2021",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pseudohypoparathyroidism is a rare genetic metabolic bone disease caused by a defect in the GNAS1 protein that leads to a decreased response to PTH. Patients present with characteristic findings of short 4th and 5th metacarpals, round facies, short stature, and symptoms of hypocalcemia.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made based on physical examination findings, serum labs, and results of the Ellsworth-Howard test.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is medical management with oral calcium and 1alpha-hydroxylated vitamin D metabolites.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Mechanism",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "PTH resistance",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "decreased target cell response to PTH",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Classification",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Type 1a - Albright hereditary osteodystrophy**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "defect in **GNAS1** (Gsα protein)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "defective gene from mother",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**upstream** defect",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "proximal to formation of cAMP",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "skeletal defects",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**short 4th, and 5th metacarpals** and metatarsals or short 4th metacarpal only",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/9029/images/pseudohypopth%20knuckles._moved.jpg",
                      "caption": ""
                    },
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/9029/images/pseudohypopth%20hand_moved.jpg",
                      "caption": ""
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "\"knuckle, knuckle, dimple, dimple\" sign on closed fist",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "differentials",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "Turner syndrome",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "text": "short 4th metacarpal only",
                              "table": null,
                              "images": [
                                {
                                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/9029/images/knuckle-dimple_moved.jpg",
                                  "caption": ""
                                }
                              ],
                              "importance": "4",
                              "children": []
                            },
                            {
                              "text": "\"knuckle, knuckle, dimple, knuckle\"",
